# Vendored ezSIFT

This directory vendors a trimmed copy of [ezSIFT](https://github.com/robertwgh/ezSIFT),
a self-contained, dependency-free SIFT implementation (Apache-2.0).

Upstream version: master @ 2018-07-10 (`robertwgh/ezSIFT`, no tagged releases).

Changes from upstream:

* `vvector.h` reduced from the full upstream macro library (1448 lines) to
  just the three macros used by `ezsift.cpp` (`MAT_DOT_VEC_3X3`,
  `DETERMINANT_3X3`, `SCALE_ADJOINT_3X3`).
* `ezsift.cpp`: dropped the `#include "timer.h"` and the unused
  `#include "vvector.h"` (now the trimmed header).
* `ezsift.h`/`ezsift.cpp`: the SIFT parameter globals are `extern` in the
  header and defined once in `ezsift.cpp`, so multiple translation units
  (the vendored core and the driver's matcher) share a single instance
  instead of getting per-TU `static` copies.
* Removed `timer.h`, `image_utility.cpp` (PGM/PPM I/O) and the example
  programs, which are not needed to build the SIFT core against raw pixel
  buffers.

The vendored sources are reformatted with the project's uncrustify config
(whitespace/brace style only; no code changes) so the `test_indent` CI check
passes. Code is otherwise identical to upstream. Upstream's own header notes
that SIFT was patented (US 6,711,293); that patent expired in March 2020.